Window surfaces let go of their textures when they are released (Minato, patch 0023).

Why: a context's default framebuffer outlives the window surface it was made current with. Its FramebufferMtl kept
the surface's render targets and a render pass whose TextureRefs held the surface's drawable, depth and stencil, and
the render encoder kept the last pass's MTLRenderPassDescriptor with the same textures, both until that context's next
render pass. A context that is not made current again (an app's SDL 2 context after a failed restore at a return)
kept a destroyed surface's depth/stencil for good: on the iPhone each return of such a game left one more
screen-sized depth/stencil alive. Now the framebuffer lets go of both when its window surface is detached, and the
encoder's cached descriptor drops its textures and visibility buffer at the end of each pass (the next pass sets them
again).
Test: graphics/tests/angle_memory_counters.mm (a window surface with depth and stencil, drawn, swapped, released and
destroyed while its context lives on: the depth/stencil count comes back).
Upstream: could be offered (a leak of a destroyed surface's textures in an idle context).

--- a/src/libANGLE/renderer/metal/FramebufferMtl.mm
+++ b/src/libANGLE/renderer/metal/FramebufferMtl.mm
@@ -144,6 +144,15 @@
 
 void FramebufferMtl::setBackbuffer(WindowSurfaceMtl *backbuffer, bool flipY)
 {
+    if (backbuffer == nullptr && mBackbuffer != nullptr)
+    {
+        // Minato (patch 0023): the context's default framebuffer outlives its window surface; let go of the
+        // surface's render targets and of the textures the cached render pass holds (its drawable, depth and
+        // stencil), which a context that is not made current again would otherwise keep for good. The next
+        // surface's attach dirties every attachment, so syncState fills both again.
+        reset();
+        mRenderPassDesc = mtl::RenderPassDesc();
+    }
     mBackbuffer      = backbuffer;
     mBackbufferFlipY = flipY;
 }
--- a/src/libANGLE/renderer/metal/mtl_command_buffer.mm
+++ b/src/libANGLE/renderer/metal/mtl_command_buffer.mm
@@ -1655,6 +1655,19 @@
     // reset state
     mRenderPassDesc = RenderPassDesc();
     mStateCache.reset();
+
+    // Minato (patch 0023): the cached descriptor lets go of the pass's textures and buffer, so that a context
+    // which encodes no other pass does not keep a destroyed surface's drawable, depth and stencil alive.
+    for (uint32_t i = 0; i < kMaxRenderTargets; ++i)
+    {
+        objCRenderPassDesc.colorAttachments[i].texture        = nil;
+        objCRenderPassDesc.colorAttachments[i].resolveTexture = nil;
+    }
+    objCRenderPassDesc.depthAttachment.texture          = nil;
+    objCRenderPassDesc.depthAttachment.resolveTexture   = nil;
+    objCRenderPassDesc.stencilAttachment.texture        = nil;
+    objCRenderPassDesc.stencilAttachment.resolveTexture = nil;
+    objCRenderPassDesc.visibilityResultBuffer           = nil;
 }
 
